      "message": "@aliceryhl@google.com -  LMK your thoughts.  This operation takes a descriptor from Reserved -\u003e Free.  If a neighbor happens to be free, then we could re-use an existing allocation in `free_tree`. Otherwise, we have to allocate a new one. Does that mean I need to introduce a `no_alloc` flavor of this method as well?",
